---
import MaterialPage from "@/components/MaterialPage.astro";
import { materialBySlug } from "@/data/materials";

const entry = materialBySlug("liquid-distort");
if (!entry) throw new Error("Unknown material");
---

<MaterialPage entry={entry}>
  <p slot="intro">
    <code>LiquidDistortMaterial</code> is the view of the tiles at the bottom of a swimming pool. A
    slow field of noise washes over the text and bends it, never quite the same way twice. Three
    uniforms: how fast the water moves, how much it bends the letters, and where in the noise to
    look when it is standing still.
  </p>

  <Fragment slot="uSpeed">
    <p>How fast the distortion moves. While it moves, <code>uSeed</code> has no effect.</p>
  </Fragment>
  <Fragment slot="uSpeed-value">
    <p>Any float, though values under <code>1.0</code> read as water rather than weather. It multiplies <code>uGlobalTime</code>; <code>0.0</code> stops the animation entirely.</p>
  </Fragment>

  <Fragment slot="uVolatility">
    <p>How much the noise displaces the letters: the distance between a legible word and an abstract one.</p>
  </Fragment>
  <Fragment slot="uVolatility-value">
    <p>Any float. <code>1.0</code> is the amount the material was designed around; going past it is allowed and gets wild quickly.</p>
  </Fragment>

  <Fragment slot="uSeed">
    <p>Where in the noise field to sample. Animation moves through the field on its own, so this only matters once <code>uSpeed</code> is <code>0.0</code> and you want a particular still frame.</p>
  </Fragment>
  <Fragment slot="uSeed-value">
    <p>Any float.</p>
  </Fragment>
</MaterialPage>
